<title>UK: SBC sets call warrants on FTSE-250 stock basket.</title>
<headline>SBC sets call warrants on FTSE-250 stock basket.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss Bank Corporation has issued five million American-style call warrants on a basket of FTSE Mid-250 shares, lead manager SBC Warburg said.</p>
<p>The basket consists of shares of Arjo Wiggins Appleton Plc</p>
<p>Firstbus Plc, Redrow Group Plc, Medeva</p>
<p>Plc and Mayflower Corp Plc. One basket is</p>
<p>controlled by one warrant.</p>
<p> STRIKE PRICE    10.0 STG		PREMIUM	13.8 PCT</p>
<p> ISSUE PRICE     1.38 STG		GEARING	7.2 TIMES</p>
<p> MATURITY DATE   11.DEC.98	     PAYDATE	20.JUN.97</p>
<p> LISTING	   LUXEMBOURG	    MIN EXER LOT 100</p>
<p>SPOT REFERENCE  10.0 STG</p>
<p>--Reuter London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
